00:13:35.240 --> 00:13:37.880
and stuff, than watching us.

00:13:37.880 --> 00:13:40.533
And my sister got hit
by a car and she died.

00:13:41.650 --> 00:13:46.360
That was, I've always taken
that upon my shoulders,

00:13:46.360 --> 00:13:47.583
that it was my fault.

00:13:48.730 --> 00:13:51.480
I just recently talked to
my brother after 30 years,

00:13:51.480 --> 00:13:54.870
after I've left home because
I was a burden to the family.

00:13:54.870 --> 00:13:57.593
I just was a bad alcoholic, always drunk.

00:13:58.750 --> 00:14:01.680
just out of control, and
my little brother told me,

00:14:01.680 --> 00:14:02.513
first thing, he said

00:14:02.513 --> 00:14:04.980
he says, Hey Tracy, it wasn't your fault.

00:14:04.980 --> 00:14:08.590
I said my fault about
what? he was about wendy.

00:14:08.590 --> 00:14:09.940
And he never even knew Wendy.

00:14:09.940 --> 00:14:12.573
He wasn't even alive when,
when wendy was alive,

00:14:14.210 --> 00:14:18.230
so he never got to know her.

00:14:18.230 --> 00:14:20.843
It kinda really touched my
heart that he said that.

00:14:21.890 --> 00:14:24.393
I talked to my brother
about every other day now,

00:14:25.320 --> 00:14:26.570
He's doing good.

00:14:26.570 --> 00:14:30.153
He's raised two daughters
since I left home.

00:14:31.610 --> 00:14:33.143
Fully grown girls.

00:14:35.710 --> 00:14:37.760
He's doing his thing, he's doing good,

00:14:37.760 --> 00:14:40.070
he's a truck driver for McDonald's.

00:14:40.070 --> 00:14:42.607
He delivers, they're
producing all that stuff,

00:14:42.607 --> 00:14:45.290
and meat and all that stuff,

00:14:45.290 --> 00:14:47.620
around Colorado,

00:14:47.620 --> 00:14:52.253
like out in Wyoming,
Nebraska and stuff like that.

00:14:53.612 --> 00:14:55.190
He makes a hundred thousand a year.

00:14:55.190 --> 00:14:56.093
He's doing good.

00:14:57.340 --> 00:14:59.180
He doesn't even look like
my little brother anymore.

00:14:59.180 --> 00:15:01.820
Matter of fact, he looks older than I do.

00:15:01.820 --> 00:15:03.643
like I said, prison preserves you.

00:15:06.610 --> 00:15:08.900
- How old were you and your sister?

00:15:08.900 --> 00:15:11.063
- I was five, She was three.

00:15:12.120 --> 00:15:14.393
She got hit, she would have been.

00:15:16.420 --> 00:15:18.310
She would have been a hell of a hell

00:15:18.310 --> 00:15:20.530
of a woman if she would have made it.

00:15:20.530 --> 00:15:24.480
She would've never been
hit my mom told me that,

00:15:24.480 --> 00:15:27.673
God had a special place
for her that he needed her,

00:15:28.739 --> 00:15:30.950
And I never could understand that.

00:15:30.950 --> 00:15:31.840
Why does he need her

00:15:31.840 --> 00:15:34.363
if he has so many dead people on his list?

00:15:38.569 --> 00:15:41.697
So that was a major loss to
our whole family because,

00:15:42.580 --> 00:15:44.990
how things pivot around females and

00:15:46.339 --> 00:15:48.473
our whole family was
just pivoted around her

00:15:48.473 --> 00:15:50.923
because she was so funny all the time and,

00:15:51.970 --> 00:15:53.860
always in a good mood.

00:15:53.860 --> 00:15:55.950
She used to come and get me food

00:15:55.950 --> 00:15:59.097
in the back window when
my mom would send me

00:15:59.097 --> 00:16:01.420
to bed without no dinner.

00:16:01.420 --> 00:16:03.310
cause I've been bad
and so on and so forth.

00:16:03.310 --> 00:16:06.010
And here she come with a
whole arm full of food for me

00:16:07.510 --> 00:16:10.103
she was, she was my sister.

00:16:12.610 --> 00:16:16.270
- Do you feel like maybe
that kind of set the set the,

00:16:16.270 --> 00:16:17.805
your path in a different direction?

00:16:17.805 --> 00:16:21.200
- Yeah that's what, I just deep inside

00:16:21.200 --> 00:16:23.830
we don't really realize
that these things we hold

00:16:23.830 --> 00:16:26.953
on to, and it makes a big
difference in our lives.

00:16:27.960 --> 00:16:28.900
That's what I've been taught

00:16:28.900 --> 00:16:30.750
going through Walden house and stuff.

00:16:32.600 --> 00:16:33.930
I held onto it.

00:16:33.930 --> 00:16:35.223
I still hold on to it,

00:16:41.311 --> 00:16:43.123
I just never really knew
how to deal with it.

00:16:43.123 --> 00:16:43.956
It's just,

00:16:46.530 --> 00:16:47.990
deep inside.

00:16:47.990 --> 00:16:48.823
it hurts .

00:16:50.577 --> 00:16:52.520
To know that,

00:16:52.520 --> 00:16:55.600
she was there at one
time and now she's gone.

00:16:55.600 --> 00:16:57.530
I've always wondered what
her life would have been.

00:16:57.530 --> 00:16:59.410
Like if she would have made it,

00:16:59.410 --> 00:17:00.853
she would still be alive.

00:17:02.480 --> 00:17:04.500
Then my brother came into the picture

00:17:04.500 --> 00:17:06.623
I kind of had resentments towards him,

00:17:07.600 --> 00:17:09.930
taking her place because
I wanted my sister back

00:17:09.930 --> 00:17:11.483
and I couldn't have her back.

00:17:15.340 --> 00:17:17.430
He knows, he knows that.

00:17:17.430 --> 00:17:19.653
But he also knows that
I love him very much.

00:17:21.870 --> 00:17:24.740
- Do you have hope now for
your, your future from here?

00:17:24.740 --> 00:17:26.937
- Well, I don't know how much future I got

00:17:26.937 --> 00:17:28.770
since am 57 years old now,

00:17:28.770 --> 00:17:31.500
I've been feeling locked
up in LA County jail

00:17:31.500 --> 00:17:33.040
since I've been 19 years old

00:17:33.040 --> 00:17:37.090
back and forth, back and
forth, back and forth to where.

00:17:37.090 --> 00:17:39.010
When they would go to
release me, I'm just like

00:17:39.010 --> 00:17:40.240
why are you guys releasing me?

00:17:40.240 --> 00:17:42.960
You're just going to bring me right back.

00:17:42.960 --> 00:17:44.963
Because I had that number.

00:17:47.580 --> 00:17:50.020
They basically want my ass out real good.

00:17:50.020 --> 00:17:50.880
I don't do nothing.

00:17:50.880 --> 00:17:53.970
I don't break into cars
and I don't sell dope.

00:17:53.970 --> 00:17:54.803
I don't do nothing.

00:17:54.803 --> 00:17:58.810
I just work my little job and
little hustle on the side.

00:17:58.810 --> 00:18:01.980
Now I got a little bit of
money to work with from SSI,

00:18:01.980 --> 00:18:03.970
So I'm going to go,

00:18:03.970 --> 00:18:06.273
do my thing and just ride dirt bikes.

00:18:07.130 --> 00:18:08.110
- Do you feel like living here

00:18:08.110 --> 00:18:11.390
in the tenderloin is a dangerous place

00:18:11.390 --> 00:18:12.470
for you to be hanging out?

00:18:12.470 --> 00:18:14.120
- No, it's not.

00:18:14.120 --> 00:18:15.413
It's not dangerous.

00:18:16.390 --> 00:18:18.160
One person can only make it dangerous

00:18:18.160 --> 00:18:20.041
to their selves, if they
don't watch their selves,

00:18:20.041 --> 00:18:22.446
if they just let their selves go and just

00:18:22.446 --> 00:18:25.884
don't give a F... about nothing
and just let themselves go

00:18:25.884 --> 00:18:28.700
and be used and abused by other people.

00:18:28.700 --> 00:18:31.500
Because other people out there
will use you and abuse you,

00:18:31.500 --> 00:18:33.963
other people in their
addictions and stuff.

00:18:37.190 --> 00:18:38.903
I feel that.

00:18:39.998 --> 00:18:41.690
What was the question again?

00:18:41.690 --> 00:18:42.550
- No, just, I just wonder

00:18:42.550 --> 00:18:44.470
if being in this
neighborhood tenderloin where

00:18:44.470 --> 00:18:46.330
there's drugs everywhere, makes it harder

00:18:46.330 --> 00:18:48.470
for you to deal with your addiction?

00:18:48.470 --> 00:18:49.583
- No, not really.

00:18:51.240 --> 00:18:52.773
It's just kinda like,

00:18:54.864 --> 00:18:55.697
I was thinking, well.

00:18:55.697 --> 00:18:57.323
now I don't have a prison number.

00:18:58.410 --> 00:18:59.930
What if I just get my motorcycle

00:18:59.930 --> 00:19:02.290
and leave in my truck,

00:19:02.290 --> 00:19:03.400
and leave.

00:19:03.400 --> 00:19:06.290
Then what am I going to do
then I'm out of this County.

00:19:06.290 --> 00:19:08.860
And if I get busted for something,

00:19:08.860 --> 00:19:10.260
they sure in hell are gonna,

00:19:12.040 --> 00:19:14.313
rack me up some years
because of my record,

00:19:15.799 --> 00:19:17.350
but with five turns and stuff,

00:19:17.350 --> 00:19:20.450
so probably better off staying here,

00:19:20.450 --> 00:19:22.860
I don't really feel that the
tenderloins have threat me

00:19:22.860 --> 00:19:25.913
because I know everybody
and everybody knows me.

00:19:28.570 --> 00:19:30.070
There's some people
out there who just flat

00:19:30.070 --> 00:19:32.290
out don't like me, but that's
their own personal feelings,

00:19:32.290 --> 00:19:35.080
I haven't done nothing to
them, and they just keep it

00:19:35.080 --> 00:19:36.083
to themselves.

00:19:38.240 --> 00:19:39.073
But survival in the
Tenderloin is very easy

00:19:39.073 --> 00:19:43.260
compared to Hollywood.

00:19:43.260 --> 00:19:46.230
Hollywood is where all these young kids go

00:19:46.230 --> 00:19:49.210
and they think they're
going to go to Hollywood

00:19:49.210 --> 00:19:51.360
and be a movie star or
a rock and roll star.

00:19:51.360 --> 00:19:53.651
And they're going to show their parents,

00:19:53.651 --> 00:19:55.819
and they're not going to
buy their parents anything

00:19:55.819 --> 00:19:56.652
and they're going to be rich.

00:19:56.652 --> 00:19:58.550
They find out that
Hollywood is just nothing

00:19:58.550 --> 00:20:00.410
but a ghetto and full of drugs

00:20:00.410 --> 00:20:04.893
and pimps and whores, gangsters and

00:20:06.720 --> 00:20:08.543
drag Queens and shit like that,

00:20:10.110 --> 00:20:11.593
the street of broken dreams.

00:20:13.860 --> 00:20:16.033
Hollywood has gotten nobody anywhere.

00:20:16.870 --> 00:20:18.220
There's a few that made it.

00:20:20.150 --> 00:20:22.410
A lot of these rock and roll,

00:20:22.410 --> 00:20:24.390
stars like Astroworld and stuff

00:20:24.390 --> 00:20:28.810
like that were on the streets, in LA.

00:20:28.810 --> 00:20:31.110
Through a lot of their songs
and their lyrics come from.

00:20:31.110 --> 00:20:33.263
it's like, living under the bridge and,

00:20:34.110 --> 00:20:36.000
dancing with Mr. Brownstone,

00:20:36.000 --> 00:20:37.250
we all know what that is.

00:20:43.290 --> 00:20:44.123
- All right, Tracy.

00:20:44.123 --> 00:20:45.300
Well, thank you so much
for sharing your story.

00:20:45.300 --> 00:20:46.230
- Yeah, no problem.

00:20:46.230 --> 00:20:48.188
And good luck with
wherever you go from here.

00:20:48.188 --> 00:20:49.021
- Thank you.

00:20:49.021 --> 00:20:49.854
- Thank you.

00:20:49.854 --> 00:20:51.054
- I've been wanting to do something

00:20:51.054 --> 00:20:51.887
like this for a long time.

00:20:51.887 --> 00:20:53.035
- Oh! Good.

00:20:53.035 --> 00:20:54.120
I think it's therapeutic now

00:20:54.120 --> 00:20:56.370
- Yeah, It's very therapeutic.

00:20:56.370 --> 00:20:58.560
- Do you ever get a chance to
talk about this with anybody?

00:20:58.560 --> 00:20:59.920
- Yeah, I talked to my caseworker

00:20:59.920 --> 00:21:01.570
my counselor all the
time about this stuff.

00:21:01.570 --> 00:21:03.920
I've talked to her so
many times and it's just,

00:21:04.830 --> 00:21:06.280
I don't know what to say anymore

00:21:06.280 --> 00:21:08.330
because I've covered everything with her.

00:21:09.330 --> 00:21:10.330
I think that's why they put me

00:21:10.330 --> 00:21:12.506
on SSI because I have so much,

00:21:12.506 --> 00:21:15.840
background of being neglected used

00:21:15.840 --> 00:21:18.343
and abused and, as a child.

00:21:19.814 --> 00:21:22.940
My mom used to beat me
pretty bad when I was

00:21:22.940 --> 00:21:24.250
before Wendy was born.

00:21:24.250 --> 00:21:28.080
And when Wendy was born,
she, she quit beating on me.

00:21:28.080 --> 00:21:31.540
So there was, no witness.

00:21:31.540 --> 00:21:33.473
So she couldn't do that.

00:21:34.810 --> 00:21:37.175
She didn't beat me really bad, but she,

00:21:37.175 --> 00:21:39.080
she beat me and locked
me in a room for days

00:21:39.080 --> 00:21:42.283
while my dad was out on the
road, truck driving and stuff.

00:21:44.698 --> 00:21:45.820
- All right.

00:21:45.820 --> 00:21:46.653
- All right.

00:21:46.653 --> 00:21:48.214
- Thank you so much.

